#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157021 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "35acfa60-3395-5f11-94f9-627499386932" :question/math-academy-id "e-7159" :question/problem "Given the sets $X = \\{ 2, 5, 7, 8 \\},$ $Y = \\{ 1, 3, 5 \\},$ and $Z = \\{ 2, 4, 6, 8 \\},$ find $X \\setminus Y,$ $Y \\setminus Z,$ and $Z \\setminus X.$" :question/worked-solution "The set $X \\setminus Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the element $5 \\in Y$ is also in $X,$ so we must remove it. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∖Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={2,5,7,8}-{1,3,5} \\\\  & ={2,7,8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Y \\setminus Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $Z.$ Note that none of the elements of $Y$ are in $Z.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∖Z & =Y-Z \\\\  & ={1,3,5}-{2,4,6,8} \\\\  & ={1,3,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Z \\setminus X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Z$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $2,8 \\in Z$ are also in $X,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z∖X & =Z-X \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8}-{2,5,7,8} \\\\  & ={4,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157022 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/id #uuid "89c94a89-21de-5a4f-a365-85701b2e4ef2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7160" :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0.$ What is $A \\setminus B?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{ 6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\setminus B$ is the *difference* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $A$ but *not* in $B.$\n\nThe elements of $A$ that are also in $B$ are $12, 24, 36$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $A.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∖B & =A-B \\\\  & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…}-{6,12,18,24,30,36,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,28,32,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "9e0d2770-a884-558f-becb-a38fe709b2a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-7167" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/96cd980d105fe04d2169f9252aa2e7e08bf57ba18cf7d7808d0c4c98c83f7767.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X.$ To represent $Y \\setminus X,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/5461edca3823f1cafd9f7b51528cd6eb1035e38f7f94c60177e369e2cdd5f350.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{ 4 \\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf1b1061-5741-59d8-a418-ceda12486338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,♢}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296424} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbbe227-245b-50c1-b20d-ddb6bfe70b54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,◻,♣,♡}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296425} {:answer/id #uuid "942a9098-88e6-5763-89c4-6b4c5ddf6534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♣}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296426} {:answer/id #uuid "fd5d56bc-47e6-5789-bd05-4f2c1efb6494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{△,◻,♠}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296427} {:answer/id #uuid "4abc2d44-192f-57ff-b76b-98726c327864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,♢,♣}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf1b1061-5741-59d8-a418-ceda12486338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,♢}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296424} :answer-field/id #uuid "551fbd58-5433-5802-8da1-414f635af75f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "faa23ac8-04a3-5479-a9d4-ad113271640a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105200" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/a50acd7e54d52f6284962cb81a5f662321b045a5d533470186719ad2a91ab18b.png)\n\nGiven the sets $Y={△,◻,♣,♡}$ and  $Z={△,◻,♡,♢,♠}$ shown above, find $Z∖Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $Z∖Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $Z$ but not $Y.$ To represent $Z∖Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Z$ but not $Y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/45a15beb8833e2974706a04b0cdfd81dcdda4b92323f0c092683b9882e53b0ea.png)\n\nThe elements $♠$ and $♢$ are in $Z$  but not $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nZ∖Y={♠,♢}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0484c05-0100-5f6a-b44b-a8e626f3ed38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,3,9,15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373756} {:answer/id #uuid "8595baa2-582e-53e8-b1f9-e6edbd6c6e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373757} {:answer/id #uuid "db7bab61-d5df-5167-96e2-027e6c413a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6,12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373758} {:answer/id #uuid "e88cf7a8-ca7f-54a4-9546-29ea0f9835bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,9,15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373759} {:answer/id #uuid "e914d248-2fb7-51b4-99a6-ccec54054f29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2,4,8,10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e88cf7a8-ca7f-54a4-9546-29ea0f9835bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,9,15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373759} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fbde483-e1f2-5193-8c02-3b4a9166b21c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0190b77-eb64-5ed1-859b-2ae7a271ba29" :question/math-academy-id "q-105216" :question/problem "If $A={3,6,9,12,15}$ and $B={2,4,6,8,10,12},$ then $A∖B=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $A∖B$ is the set of all elements belonging to $A$ but *not* $B.$ Note that the elements $6,12\\in B$ are also in $A,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∖B & =A-B \\\\  & ={3,6,9,12,15}-{2,4,6,8,10,12} \\\\  & ={3,9,15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de86a42-64e6-58cb-987c-7a350f6c40ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,4,8,12,16,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373763} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c36e4b-22da-58a0-acd9-04e19f5208f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373764} {:answer/id #uuid "234fb81d-a0c6-5a68-a0cb-b6828e28a816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2,4,10,14,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373765} {:answer/id #uuid "d047cf23-b809-57ec-a322-b055907c1fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,12,16,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373766} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8c2b53-47eb-52ac-a867-796887360db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,2,6,10,14,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8c36e4b-22da-58a0-acd9-04e19f5208f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373764} :answer-field/id #uuid "0332e596-2c87-56c9-b761-09e0ed4f7f2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8f8cb276-b659-562e-b6db-d0ae01383b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105230" :question/problem "Let $S$  be the set of all multiples of $2$ greater than $0$ and let $T$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $T∖S?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $2$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nS={2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nT={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $T∖S$ is the *difference* of $T$ and $S,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $T$ but *not* in $S.$\n\nThe elements of $T$ that are also in $S$ are $4,8,12,16,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $4$). So, we must remove these elements from $T.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T∖S & ={4,8,12,16,…}-{2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9e32c4d-ef08-51e0-b785-e0d656e8933d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373770} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a29fb7-86a6-53dc-9cc6-a3c99577e899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2,4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373771} {:answer/id #uuid "cea9c90a-5b39-5002-bd45-f8bd80e7419c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373772} {:answer/id #uuid "f95c85e8-c983-5c97-9690-bbb8a0acdcd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373773} {:answer/id #uuid "228de5e7-3545-5729-8d1a-5e6fbdafb9db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5a29fb7-86a6-53dc-9cc6-a3c99577e899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2,4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373771} :answer-field/id #uuid "10c72458-0179-53ff-a62d-d250090e825d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3063079f-ee07-546e-b8b1-466892d97610" :question/math-academy-id "q-1225" :question/problem "If $X={1,3,5,7}$ and $Y={1,2,3,4},$ then $Y-X=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $Y-X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $1,3\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y-X & ={1,2,3,4}-{1,3,5,7} \\\\  & ={2,4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a38e175f-eb61-52d6-a84c-818bda19ad08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373777} {:answer/id #uuid "2f44025a-dbc5-5b01-a654-88c3658433c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,5,10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373778} {:answer/id #uuid "90954c9d-8ad1-5538-8628-b14fa769ec14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373779} {:answer/id #uuid "ca89cfd9-5519-5a67-b266-54317959089c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373780} {:answer/id #uuid "84e8592d-c1cc-5855-a21c-044ec2895f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-2,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f44025a-dbc5-5b01-a654-88c3658433c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,5,10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373778} :answer-field/id #uuid "607f344d-06bc-52c2-ab72-53163671b476" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39717e4d-c7d4-5afc-8012-4f6b4b25dff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-1226" :question/problem "If $C={-3,-1,0,5,10}$ and $D={-2,-1,0,1}$, then $C∖D=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $C∖D$ is the set of all elements belonging to $C$ but *not* $D.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in D$ are also in $C,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & ={-3,-1,0,5,10}-{-2,-1,0,1} \\\\  & ={-3,5,10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a620074-8937-5edb-b91d-c86438c99280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373784} {:answer/id #uuid "e695d5c5-aab7-5b16-a321-518de591a57a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,5,10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373785} {:answer/id #uuid "454600ac-b3ab-5858-80c8-77c0cbe9c3cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373786} {:answer/id #uuid "121f254c-0a80-5e5f-84d7-a2e0859acea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373787} {:answer/id #uuid "790d01bc-9cd5-5d7d-a2ba-959438536052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-2,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "790d01bc-9cd5-5d7d-a2ba-959438536052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-2,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373788} :answer-field/id #uuid "44514e72-9659-5340-baa1-4524a963923f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13d98e6d-2242-52db-95f5-9d692398076e" :question/math-academy-id "q-1227" :question/problem "If $C={-3,-1,0,5,10}$ and $D={-2,-1,0,1},$ then $D∖C=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $D∖C$ is the set of all elements belonging to $D$ but *not* $C.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in C$ are also in $D,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∖C & =D-C \\\\  & ={-2,-1,0,1}-{-3,-1,0,5,10} \\\\  & ={-2,1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b4067ec-5740-591e-9ff3-7373070b8280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5, 10, 12, 15, 20, 22, 25, 30, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155489} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c7f211-a458-52a6-a5c3-cc536d2619d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155490} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc000c3-47c5-5a3b-bea8-938125ac8863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155491} {:answer/id #uuid "e93086d2-41f8-5f2a-bf13-bf57ada29922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5, 15, 25, 35, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155492} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3a235b-1bfe-51ad-8dfc-250681d8cf1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, 5, 15, 25, 35, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e93086d2-41f8-5f2a-bf13-bf57ada29922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5, 15, 25, 35, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155492} :answer-field/id #uuid "13dd5650-ba21-5510-8ce8-7dd096da61c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94581c78-fe62-5c44-8cc0-1ddd120bd04f" :question/math-academy-id "q-36195" :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $10$ greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0.$ What is $B∖A?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={10,20,30,40,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B∖A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∖A & =B-A \\\\  & ={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,…}-{10,20,30,40,…} \\\\  & ={5,15,25,35,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "666c0a71-adc8-5394-81f5-8cc06b52fec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,16,20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373791} {:answer/id #uuid "8b178d8c-1168-5b65-b567-d2c3c29f44c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,2,3,4,8,12,16,20,24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373792} {:answer/id #uuid "7dbe8cbf-eb50-5600-8a2d-ffab3dd676fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,2,3,16,20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373793} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f9dd83-9729-55a6-a0df-a008a66ab670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373794} {:answer/id #uuid "f3406b5a-3535-5809-81cf-1b5e8b1ff8d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,12,24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "666c0a71-adc8-5394-81f5-8cc06b52fec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,16,20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373791} :answer-field/id #uuid "110bfe90-16e3-5e51-9535-664110aac1f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59e8e75c-5f6b-5b3e-accd-ed5dccbc84b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-80869" :question/problem "If $C={1,2,3,4,8,12,24}$ and $D={0,4,8,12,16,20,24},$ then $D∖C=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $D∖C$ is the set of all elements belonging to $D$ but *not* $C.$ Note that the elements $4,8,12,24\\in C$ are also in $D,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∖C & =D-C \\\\  & ={0,4,8,12,16,20,24}-{1,2,3,4,8,12,24} \\\\  & ={0,16,20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfd2fced-4366-5e8e-84e6-0b9bbe451fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373798} {:answer/id #uuid "ca41bfe1-2185-5f8b-8871-3f8a6ffa3082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373799} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc97d2a-2bb3-50cb-9609-da058b25ee34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15,30,45,60,75,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373800} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbf96d1-db2a-5f99-af14-f66f0b10ea22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373801} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc7be85-8623-5c7b-a5b1-4833b2027095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,15,25,35,45,55,65,75,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca41bfe1-2185-5f8b-8871-3f8a6ffa3082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373799} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f57eac1-42c3-57be-8825-0fb0d6c2c319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e51fe277-17dd-59c2-bd43-427728072d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-80876" :question/problem "Let $C$  be the set of all multiples of $10$ greater than $0$ and let $D$  be the the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0.$ What is $C∖D?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nC={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nD={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $C∖D$ is the *difference* of $C$ and $D,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $C$ but *not* in $D.$\n\nThe elements of $C$ that are also in $D$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & ={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}-{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ff5d091-4d8d-5c45-a247-2c4b1cfd19dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f,e,r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373805} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ba3ac6-3da3-5141-8a4d-f00b45667bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{m,n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373806} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6bc3e5-f849-5b86-8cf0-5063a2a6b454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{d,i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373807} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc476db-7270-5054-b96b-3189285e6f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{r,l,d,i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373808} {:answer/id #uuid "789ab456-2edf-5599-9408-d54aff836bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "789ab456-2edf-5599-9408-d54aff836bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373809} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d607d5-c0be-59c8-bb35-e771ea6d401e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4745e1e-8ed1-5691-b0d7-67c4f8ae24ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-81518" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/a2cee4b60fe7cf45df5cca5c0d513c38f6639b08486272d9cb4e605b8359935c.png)\n\nGiven the sets $A={d,i,f,e,r}$ and $B={f,e,r,a,k},$ find $B∖A.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $B∖A$ consists of all the elements that are in $B$ but not $A.$ To represent $B∖A,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $B$ but not $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/7ec40584f82d7bd01aa7323ffb9cc4a53d631b74ea1d312d1b4141eb5da8d0d9.png)\n\nThe elements $a$ and $k$ are in $B$ but not $A.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nB∖A={a,k}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "476797a6-58b7-5bd7-82bd-148c80ccc45a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{p,a,s,t,e,l}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373812} {:answer/id #uuid "3cba5e5b-827c-5a33-86a8-ceb6c7166b82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t,e,l}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373813} {:answer/id #uuid "a8363fa0-ed20-59fb-9fc1-e0eb8e5363fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,s,w,d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373814} {:answer/id #uuid "2122c1e6-7992-5109-9d78-8399656b2118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{p,o,r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373815} {:answer/id #uuid "1b70009e-9fb3-5b18-8d36-38b9a3b9bac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t,e,l,a,s,w,d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cba5e5b-827c-5a33-86a8-ceb6c7166b82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t,e,l}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373813} :answer-field/id #uuid "0da04137-6076-5e57-81ad-8d1735ed8361" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07d2156e-07bf-5126-9d10-39040c798dc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-81695" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/3b539190899ca580528fdbf7b5d3ef9925ade29f97f4b2f96b0f1394743f40a8.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S={p,a,s,w,o,r,d}$ and $T={p,o,r,t,e,l},$ find $T∖S.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $T∖S$ consists of all the elements that are in $T$ but not $S.$ To represent $T∖S,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $T$ but not $S.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/c718918667c5076f8696ea98f453ff17f005d5f7cace87bd863be309fac28d72.png)\n\nThe elements $t,e,$ and $l$ are in $T$ but not $S.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nT∖S={t,e,l}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c145ff56-c0d2-57cc-a615-275bca74d3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x,y,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373819} {:answer/id #uuid "028ed475-9c2f-515b-8f75-5deb9622f1d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t,m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373820} {:answer/id #uuid "441b2cdf-450e-541c-a3af-2a1a4546ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{c,e,k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373821} {:answer/id #uuid "b65c072a-6b79-52c0-b08b-1080a47ea624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,s,r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373822} {:answer/id #uuid "277fa6be-675a-5cc8-9a91-8b3ba2204251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t,m,x,y,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "441b2cdf-450e-541c-a3af-2a1a4546ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{c,e,k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373821} :answer-field/id #uuid "12057daf-a482-5874-8712-79b8b4f34925" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7234e8f3-4974-5d8f-b94d-29e990e159ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-81754" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/23cb8614a030b7f3ff90d3a31264f5c78b50e9d4c8f0f810db21fde668a42c16.png)\n\nGiven the sets $A={c,e,a,s,r,k}$ and $B={a,s,t,r,m},$ find $A∖B.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $A∖B$ consists of all the elements that are in $A$ but not $B.$ To represent $A∖B,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $A$ but not $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/213ede994f6a88d5a6235d3b12f07090e8cb64568c9e0cbd4051246e2e90a8b8.png)\n\nThe elements $c,e,$ and $k$ are in $A$ but not $B.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nA∖B={c,e,k}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a9bf1c3-c25e-546d-bf50-f506b6cb2bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,16,20,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296501} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5b5b4e-290f-541c-ba2f-6ba2982c59cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{12,24…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296502} {:answer/id #uuid "d4685bed-f4c4-5ce4-b803-08ec3f7b9daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,6,9,15,18,21,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296503} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3343f8-3a82-58af-bc78-065391a8604e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,4,6,8,9,15,16,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296504} {:answer/id #uuid "0db51cb2-8bf8-5b33-a63b-bc763b47289f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,3,6,9,15,18,21,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a9bf1c3-c25e-546d-bf50-f506b6cb2bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,16,20,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296501} :answer-field/id #uuid "af625279-b9b8-5e8b-9297-c5d5fbef4f97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4c54f56-ff83-5c5e-b062-1e1004f84f48" :question/math-academy-id "q-81766" :question/problem "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $B-A?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}-{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e8bdc02-f11c-5a11-b55e-625f43d09434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373826} {:answer/id #uuid "32a75745-0add-57d6-a68c-dbbf69d2cc1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373827} {:answer/id #uuid "9e57f06c-d18f-56c8-9629-fffc7a4a6053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,3,5,7,9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373828} {:answer/id #uuid "87e937eb-3ec9-557a-8fa1-814f89addfbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,7,9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373829} {:answer/id #uuid "b17c5dad-b027-5b9f-8e43-32c00318a0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87e937eb-3ec9-557a-8fa1-814f89addfbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,7,9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373829} :answer-field/id #uuid "01e4fba1-2865-5f6a-92b9-05df7dbed1c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6707a032-a443-512f-b238-b5bd0a3b0a0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-86701" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/96962d11526f30beee45b85aac92808518352d7b79b4b4f2e4a7351ddd9fe17e.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S={5,7,9}$ and $T={0,1,3},$find $S∖T.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $S∖T$ consists of all the elements that are in $S$ but not $T.$ To represent $S∖T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $S$ but not $T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/be1caefc99bea5d4dde0ba272a208dd8f587156029ce37df483e40cd5f6121d2.png)\n\nAll elements of $S$ are not in $T.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nS∖T={5,7,9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "606d1dc5-1b35-5479-b925-c7ac318780b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,4,16,64,256,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373833} {:answer/id #uuid "f16879e0-88f6-5e79-bf20-f2b5219274b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373834} {:answer/id #uuid "82b084e7-de65-5ef1-ae59-2986caad96ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,16,64,256,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373835} {:answer/id #uuid "9da72b15-4218-5bff-8cd6-4b49ad3b4969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373836} {:answer/id #uuid "a256e1bd-de05-59ae-a0e1-2dc375843e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,4,8,16,32,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9da72b15-4218-5bff-8cd6-4b49ad3b4969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373836} :answer-field/id #uuid "089d9403-e7b6-54bd-a559-438c7b929d25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0434064c-21b0-5964-ac5a-a3966fbb623a" :question/math-academy-id "q-86705" :question/problem "Let $E$  be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $2$ and let $F$  be  the set of all non-negative integer powers of $4.$  What is $F-E?$" :question/worked-solution "The powers of $2$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nE={1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, the powers of $4$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nF={1,4,16,64,256,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $F-E$ is the *difference* of $F$ and $E,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $F$ but *not* in $E.$\n\nAll elements of $F$ are also in $E.$  So, we must remove these elements from $F.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F-E & ={1,4,16,64,256,…}-{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
